  "body": "### Reproduction steps\n\n1. Create .devcontainer folder.\n2. Create devcontainer.json with contents:\n```json\n{\n  \"use_podman\": true\n}\n```\n3. Start zed\n4.When prompted choose: \"Yes, Open in Container\" (to start the devcontainer.\n\n### Current vs. Expected behavior\n\n### Current Behaviour\n\n#### Bug 1\n<img width=\"443\" height=\"213\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2e3f2c3c-eba6-4ca5-8f87-265b7cf16ef1\" />\n\n#### Bug2 ?\nNo log entry that says that docker was not found (which was the case in previous Versions).\n\nNote: If I remove the option \"use_podman\", I DO get a log entry:\n`2026-03-16T10:41:55+01:00 ERROR [recent_projects::remote_servers] Failed to start dev container: DockerNotAvailable`, but NOT when `use_podman` is set to true.\n\n#### Important Context\nPodman Option \"Docker Compatibility Mode\" is enabled. Commands like `docker run` DO work in the zed terminal (powershell).\n\n### Expected Behaviour\nZed uses podman to start the devcontainer.\n\n\n### Zed version and system specs\n\nZed 0.227.1 \n9f9b707d39d62468d4cdaed2d8eb95a847da4cf9\n\n0.227.1+stable.199.9f9b707d39d62468d4cdaed2d8eb95a847da4cf9\n\n### Attach Zed log file\n\n<details><summary>Zed.log</summary>\n\n<!-- Paste your log inside the code block. -->\n```log\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Relevant Zed settings\n\n<details><summary>settings.json</summary>\n\n<!-- Paste your settings inside the code block. -->\n```json\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### Relevant Keymap\n\n<details><summary>keymap.json</summary>\n\n<!-- Paste your keymap file inside the code block. -->\n```json\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n### (for AI issues) Model provider details\n\n_No response_\n\n### If you are using WSL on Windows, what flavor of Linux are you using?\n\nUbuntu",
